From 518945a26730178dec53e2f1a9e3a3decf74400d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:04:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: Dolby Vision page in the player information, OSD
 button

Checking Dolby Vision playback meant opening the OSD, then its settings,
then "Player process info", and even there only the profile was shown.

- A "Dolby Vision" page in the player information, shown for Dolby
  Vision sources and focused when the dialog opens during one. It reads
  the hades.dv.* Home window properties published by the DV bridge:
  output in use (native TV-led, or the ordinary output and why), profile
  and layers (BL + EL FEL/MEL, or BL), L1 min / avg / max and L6
  MaxCLL / MaxFALL in cd/m2, L2 trims, HDMI link mode and signal, what
  the TV offers, and the last 10-s window (frames shown and failed,
  longest gap, L5 offsets, frames with changed L1).
- A button in the video OSD, next to Information, that opens the player
  information directly (texture osd/fullscreen/buttons/processinfo.png,
  added by the build: GNU patch cannot carry binary diffs).
- Strings 31650-31675, with es_AR, es_ES and es_MX translations.
